.docname {Documentation Build}
.include {docs}

.glossary
    | Word | Meaning | Example |
    |---|---|---|
    | Quarkdown | A Markdown superset that compiles to HTML, with functions written `.name {arg}` | `.mermaid`, `.box {Title} type:{warning}` |
    | Function call | A word after a dot, read by Quarkdown as a call | `.glossary` |
    | Component | A reusable block: one `.function` plus its style and script | `components/glossary.qd` |
    | Slot | The indented body passed to a component | The table under `.glossary` |
    | Strict mode | Quarkdown stops on the first error instead of printing it on the page | `--strict` |
    | Sidebar | The left menu, written by hand in `_nav.qd` | Section "Services" |
    | Top nav | The links in the header, in `config/site.qd` | "API", "Test Coverage" |
    | Swagger UI | A page that renders an OpenAPI file as browsable docs | `api/index.html?spec=twin.yaml` |
    | GitHub Pages | Static hosting for the published site | Branch `gh-pages` |

The guide is written in Quarkdown under `documentation/`. `just docs build` turns it, plus the OpenAPI files in `api/`, into a static site in `landing-page/`. CI runs the same recipe and publishes the result to GitHub Pages.

`landing-page/` is build output only: ignored by git, rebuilt from zero every time.

---

## Layout of `documentation/`

| Path | Holds |
|---|---|
| `main.qd` | The entry file and home page |
| `_setup.qd` | Included by every page: site settings |
| `_nav.qd` | The sidebar |
| `config/site.qd` | Title, language, theme, header links, footer, the script loader, the component list |
| `config/standalone.qd` | Used by `reference/` pages instead of `docs`: no side menus |
| `components/` | One `<name>.qd` per component, all listed in `components/index.qd` |
| `style/tokens.css` | Colours, sizes and fonts as variables |
| `style/quarkdown.css` | Every rule that names Quarkdown's own HTML |
| `scripts/` | `quarkdown-dom.js` plus page-wide scripts: `nav-collapse.js`, `table-scroll.js`, `toc-spy.js` |
| `docs/<section>/*.qd` | The pages |

`main.qd`, `_setup.qd` and `_nav.qd` sit at the root on purpose: Quarkdown's `docs` library looks for them beside the entry file, and refuses to read outside the entry file's folder.

### How a page is put together

.mermaid
    flowchart TD
        P["docs/toolchain/linting.qd"] --> I["include docs"]
        I --> S["_setup.qd"]
        I --> N["_nav.qd, sidebar"]
        S --> C["config/site.qd"]
        C --> X["components/index.qd, every component"]
        C --> L["script tag for theme/crowdvision.js"]
        C --> A["actions bar, footer"]

- Every page starts with `.docname {Title}` and `.include {docs}`.
- The `.docname` must equal the page's label in `_nav.qd`.

---

## Two layers that may name Quarkdown's HTML

Quarkdown's generated HTML (class names, `data-role` attributes) can change in any release. Only two files may name it:

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `style/quarkdown.css` | All CSS aimed at Quarkdown's elements |
| `scripts/quarkdown-dom.js` | `window.CV`: functions like `CV.tocLinks()` and `CV.content()` that find elements for every other script |

A Quarkdown upgrade then touches two files, not every component. The build enforces it (step 3 below).

---

## `just docs build`, step by step

.mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant D as Developer or CI
        participant J as just<br/>just/docs.just
        participant L as check-docs-links.sh
        participant Q as quarkdown
        participant O as landing-page/
        participant M as docs-meta.py
        D->>J: just docs build
        J->>J: check-version: installed quarkdown vs the mise pin
        J->>J: check-layers: Quarkdown names outside the two files?
        J->>L: sh scripts/check-docs-links.sh
        L-->>J: every page in a nav, every spec linked
        J->>O: rm -rf landing-page
        J->>Q: quarkdown c documentation/main.qd --out the staging folder, native content allowed, strict
        Q-->>O: staging folder, subfolder Developer-Guide
        J->>O: lift the staged guide folder to the root, delete the staging folder
        J->>O: append tokens.css and quarkdown.css to theme/theme.css
        J->>O: concatenate the four scripts into theme/crowdvision.js
        J->>M: python3 scripts/docs-meta.py landing-page/theme/page-meta.json
        M-->>O: last change of every page, and the version
        J->>O: copy the Swagger page and the YAML specs into landing-page/api/

| Step | What happens | Real value |
|---|---|---|
| 2 | The installed Quarkdown must be the pinned one | `QUARKDOWN_VERSION = "2.7.0"` in `.mise.toml` |
| 3 | Search `components/`, `scripts/` and `style/tokens.css` for `body.quarkdown`, `.quarkdown-docs` or `data-role=`, skipping `quarkdown-dom.js` | One hit fails the build and lists the file |
| 4–5 | See "Reachable pages" below | |
| 6 | Start from empty: no stale page survives a rename | |
| 7 | `--strict`: the first error stops the build. `--allow native-content` lets `.html` blocks through | Exit code `66` on a bad function call |
| 8 | Quarkdown always writes into `<out>/<docname>/` | `Developer-Guide/`, from `main.qd`'s `.docname` |
| 9 | The guide is the whole site, so its folder is lifted to the root | `landing-page/index.html` |
| 10 | Order matters: tokens first, so `quarkdown.css` can use the variables | |
| 11 | One file, loaded by every page through `config/site.qd` | `quarkdown-dom.js` first: the others call `CV` |
| 12–13 | `git log -1` per page, `--follow --diff-filter=M` so a move is not an edit; version from `.release-please-manifest.json` | Shape, made-up values: `{"telemetry-schema":{"path":"documentation/docs/packages/telemetry-schema.qd","commit":"ebb813f2","date":"2026-11-02"},"_version":"v0.3.1-alpha"}` |
| 14 | Specs are copied after the guide | `landing-page/api/twin.yaml` |

`just docs serve` builds, then serves `landing-page/` at port 8080 with `live-server`. `just docs preview` runs Quarkdown's own watcher, guide only.

### Reachable pages

`scripts/check-docs-links.sh` stops a page or a spec from publishing with nothing linking to it.

.mermaid
    flowchart TD
        A["each page under documentation/docs"] --> B{"path in _nav.qd or config/site.qd?"}
        B -- no --> E1["error: linked from neither"]
        B -- yes --> C{"file named api.qd?"}
        C -- yes --> E2["error: the api/ specs would overwrite it"]
        C -- no --> OK1["fine"]
        S["each spec in api/"] --> D{"spec=name.yaml in api-reference.qd?"}
        D -- no --> E3["error: spec not linked"]
        D -- yes --> OK2["fine"]

- A page belongs in **one** of the two navigations. `reference/` pages live in the top nav only.
- Quarkdown names each output folder after the file name. A page `api.qd` would build to `landing-page/api/`, then be overwritten by the specs at step 14, with no error.

---

## The API reference

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `api/*.yaml` | One OpenAPI file per area: `auth`, `twin`, `telemetry`, `notification`, `contracts`, `error` |
| `api/index.html` | Swagger UI from `unpkg.com/swagger-ui-dist@5`. Reads `?spec=` from the address and loads that file next to it |
| `docs/reference/api-reference.qd` | The table of links, `../api/index.html?spec=twin.yaml` |

**Example.** A click on "Twin Service API" opens `api/index.html?spec=twin.yaml`. The script reads `spec`, and Swagger UI fetches `twin.yaml` from the same folder. With no `spec`, the page says "No API definition specified".

---

## CI and publishing

.mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant G as GitHub
        participant C as ci-docs.yml
        participant P as cd-documentation.yml
        participant H as GitHub Pages
        G->>C: pull request, through ci-gate.yml
        C->>C: checkout with full history
        C->>C: read QUARKDOWN_VERSION, install it and just 1.42.4
        C->>C: just docs build
        G->>P: push to master touching docs, api, the scripts or the mise pins
        P->>P: same install, just docs build
        P->>H: peaceiris/actions-gh-pages publishes landing-page/

- **One recipe.** Both workflows call `just docs build`. Listing the steps again in YAML is how the specs or the portal would silently stop being published.
- **Full history** (`fetch-depth: 0`): `docs-meta.py` needs `git log`, which a shallow clone does not have.
- **One version.** `setup-quarkdown` installs the latest release when given none. Reading the pin from `.mise.toml` stops an upstream release from changing the HTML the theme styles.
- `concurrency: deploy-docs` with `cancel-in-progress`: a newer push replaces a running deploy.

---

## Known traps

| Trap | What happens | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `.word(` in text or in a Mermaid block | Quarkdown reads `.lock(` in `gate(b1).lock()` as a function call. Strict mode stops: `Unresolved reference: lock` | Write `lock gate(b1)`, or keep the call inside inline code in prose |
| A link inside a component slot | A relative link resolves from the **component's** file, not the page: `../packages/x.qd` inside `.glossary` fails with `Cannot resolve subdocument link` | No links in `.glossary` or `.box`; on the components page write `../docs/...` |
| A page missing from both navigations | `check-docs-links.sh` fails before Quarkdown runs | Add it to `_nav.qd`, or to `config/site.qd` for `reference/` |
| A script holding elements found at load | Quarkdown rebuilds parts of the page after Mermaid renders, so saved elements go stale. The page outline stopped following the scroll this way | Look elements up again through `CV` each time |
| Quarkdown names in a component | `check-layers` fails | Add a function to `quarkdown-dom.js` or a rule to `quarkdown.css` |
| Another Quarkdown version installed | `check-version` fails with both numbers | Install the pinned build, or change the pin and recheck the two layer files |

---

## Adding a page

1. Create `documentation/docs/<section>/<name>.qd`, starting with `.docname {Title}` and `.include {docs}`.
2. Add `- [Title](./docs/<section>/<name>.qd)` to `_nav.qd`, under its section.
3. Link other pages with paths relative to the page: `../services/telemetry.qd`.
4. Run `just docs build`, then `just docs serve` to look at it.

See also: [Documentation Components](components.qd), [just](just.qd), [CI](ci.qd).
